[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186083240 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-21abfc2b-1c65-57da-8fcf-53cc0cb791f0" "question-7c906060-00dc-59ed-b471-aa166bd736b1" "question-20010f38-3e5e-5e3e-a89d-c3c51d40861a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-21abfc2b-1c65-57da-8fcf-53cc0cb791f0" :question/id #uuid "21abfc2b-1c65-57da-8fcf-53cc0cb791f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-6840" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}=-\\frac{3}{t\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+1}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =-\\,\\frac{3}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}+1} \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{3}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\cdot 0+1} \\\\  & =-\\,3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3bfbeb97-b5a7-5edb-811c-c6fd832edf47"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3bfbeb97-b5a7-5edb-811c-c6fd832edf47" :answer-field/id #uuid "3bfbeb97-b5a7-5edb-811c-c6fd832edf47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e0c0fa7e-1c3b-5c73-8f6c-dd538719b8ec" :answer-field/choices ["answer-16e9c511-8886-5f56-8ee7-6556baca60f7" "answer-e0c0fa7e-1c3b-5c73-8f6c-dd538719b8ec" "answer-9f3946a4-4840-5c17-bc49-b6cd5ef2faaf" "answer-2ef85eba-7368-57c1-8685-8d542b3d4d4c" "answer-f30dcc98-6482-51c6-8828-44cf84a10887"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16e9c511-8886-5f56-8ee7-6556baca60f7" :answer/id #uuid "16e9c511-8886-5f56-8ee7-6556baca60f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0c0fa7e-1c3b-5c73-8f6c-dd538719b8ec" :answer/id #uuid "e0c0fa7e-1c3b-5c73-8f6c-dd538719b8ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f3946a4-4840-5c17-bc49-b6cd5ef2faaf" :answer/id #uuid "9f3946a4-4840-5c17-bc49-b6cd5ef2faaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{1}{3\\pi +1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ef85eba-7368-57c1-8685-8d542b3d4d4c" :answer/id #uuid "2ef85eba-7368-57c1-8685-8d542b3d4d4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{1}{\\pi +1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f30dcc98-6482-51c6-8828-44cf84a10887" :answer/id #uuid "f30dcc98-6482-51c6-8828-44cf84a10887" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{3}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7c906060-00dc-59ed-b471-aa166bd736b1" :question/id #uuid "7c906060-00dc-59ed-b471-aa166bd736b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-20987" :question/problem "![](images/b1/b165889c6169a417f4d56f544aec8a049685693ff2b01ea13d51a9f4d841be4c.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx={t}^{3}-t,\\,y={t}^{2}-4,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=3.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{t}^{2}-1,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2t}{3{t}^{2}-1}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=3$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{2\\cdot 3}{3({3}^{2})-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{27-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4988bf56-303b-59a6-9f79-eb24f4974217"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4988bf56-303b-59a6-9f79-eb24f4974217" :answer-field/id #uuid "4988bf56-303b-59a6-9f79-eb24f4974217" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8f46d6ae-1324-5217-a00b-81747e796c9b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5f5471cf-39c9-57da-8b25-92ea610ee7b8" "answer-1b2ee053-4ac9-5907-8967-107610ee1cf5" "answer-c7633560-8973-5686-88cd-7be9b7f74ba3" "answer-8f46d6ae-1324-5217-a00b-81747e796c9b" "answer-3cf9859f-7190-5b4a-9b1c-0d332479daeb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f5471cf-39c9-57da-8b25-92ea610ee7b8" :answer/id #uuid "5f5471cf-39c9-57da-8b25-92ea610ee7b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b2ee053-4ac9-5907-8967-107610ee1cf5" :answer/id #uuid "1b2ee053-4ac9-5907-8967-107610ee1cf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7633560-8973-5686-88cd-7be9b7f74ba3" :answer/id #uuid "c7633560-8973-5686-88cd-7be9b7f74ba3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f46d6ae-1324-5217-a00b-81747e796c9b" :answer/id #uuid "8f46d6ae-1324-5217-a00b-81747e796c9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3cf9859f-7190-5b4a-9b1c-0d332479daeb" :answer/id #uuid "3cf9859f-7190-5b4a-9b1c-0d332479daeb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-20010f38-3e5e-5e3e-a89d-c3c51d40861a" :question/id #uuid "20010f38-3e5e-5e3e-a89d-c3c51d40861a" :question/math-academy-id "q-20989" :question/problem "![](images/0b/0bd043f0ff9b6cc575d7912776bd0aaa41dc161b32304115cf6c8dedba86f81a.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,y=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{8}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}{6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}=-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡2t.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =-\\,\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{4}{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ce157c42-a9a4-5ec7-af0b-682ed5561091"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ce157c42-a9a4-5ec7-af0b-682ed5561091" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce157c42-a9a4-5ec7-af0b-682ed5561091" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-389a5696-c840-56e0-8558-733de5240472" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f37683f8-f240-5221-9235-386d2ba6e331" "answer-98cc3f2f-f840-5de8-acdb-83f201a4880d" "answer-389a5696-c840-56e0-8558-733de5240472" "answer-aaab6afb-3ab3-5a9f-849c-a2ad0e12fb8e" "answer-4017febd-50d6-5503-af7a-ff948aace873"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f37683f8-f240-5221-9235-386d2ba6e331" :answer/id #uuid "f37683f8-f240-5221-9235-386d2ba6e331" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98cc3f2f-f840-5de8-acdb-83f201a4880d" :answer/id #uuid "98cc3f2f-f840-5de8-acdb-83f201a4880d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-389a5696-c840-56e0-8558-733de5240472" :answer/id #uuid "389a5696-c840-56e0-8558-733de5240472" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aaab6afb-3ab3-5a9f-849c-a2ad0e12fb8e" :answer/id #uuid "aaab6afb-3ab3-5a9f-849c-a2ad0e12fb8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4017febd-50d6-5503-af7a-ff948aace873" :answer/id #uuid "4017febd-50d6-5503-af7a-ff948aace873" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083243 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ef5ed0c9-8fa3-5025-804c-fe51ae9e2b6d" "question-08b30b3b-db11-543f-b5eb-089393bd6bb2" "question-df476431-ab3a-5147-98f8-ef5f1e16d04c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ef5ed0c9-8fa3-5025-804c-fe51ae9e2b6d" :question/id #uuid "ef5ed0c9-8fa3-5025-804c-fe51ae9e2b6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-15477" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx={sec}^{2}⁡t,\\,y={csc}^{3}⁡t,\\,0<t<\\frac{\\pi }{2},\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2{sec}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-3{csc}^{3}⁡t\\operatorname{cot}⁡t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{-3{csc}^{3}⁡t\\operatorname{cot}⁡t}{2{sec}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t} \\\\  & =-3{csc}^{3}⁡t\\operatorname{cot}⁡t(\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cot}⁡t}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\,{csc}^{3}⁡t{cot}^{2}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{1}{{sin}^{3}⁡t})(\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡t}{{sin}^{2}⁡t}){cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{{cos}^{4}⁡t}{{sin}^{5}⁡t}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡t{cot}^{4}⁡t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}){cot}^{4}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\, \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-940ee680-1c54-57c6-9fe1-a296cc68c0ad"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-940ee680-1c54-57c6-9fe1-a296cc68c0ad" :answer-field/id #uuid "940ee680-1c54-57c6-9fe1-a296cc68c0ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b432d866-9d8e-5893-a7c9-658ab974d99b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5348801e-a631-5d23-93d5-012769dd8d19" "answer-b432d866-9d8e-5893-a7c9-658ab974d99b" "answer-0825b7a7-74a7-5935-86cd-1b0bba712bd3" "answer-d843b8af-69d9-5879-a337-8dde5a272ce0" "answer-600a5309-7bc1-513f-8449-5d85d2a64fd0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5348801e-a631-5d23-93d5-012769dd8d19" :answer/id #uuid "5348801e-a631-5d23-93d5-012769dd8d19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b432d866-9d8e-5893-a7c9-658ab974d99b" :answer/id #uuid "b432d866-9d8e-5893-a7c9-658ab974d99b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0825b7a7-74a7-5935-86cd-1b0bba712bd3" :answer/id #uuid "0825b7a7-74a7-5935-86cd-1b0bba712bd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d843b8af-69d9-5879-a337-8dde5a272ce0" :answer/id #uuid "d843b8af-69d9-5879-a337-8dde5a272ce0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-600a5309-7bc1-513f-8449-5d85d2a64fd0" :answer/id #uuid "600a5309-7bc1-513f-8449-5d85d2a64fd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-08b30b3b-db11-543f-b5eb-089393bd6bb2" :question/id #uuid "08b30b3b-db11-543f-b5eb-089393bd6bb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-15470" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx={e}^{t}-{e}^{-t},\\,y=t{e}^{t},\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)={e}^{t}+{e}^{-t},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=(t+1){e}^{t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{(t+1){e}^{t}}{{e}^{t}+{e}^{-t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+t}{1+{e}^{-2t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=0,$ the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{1+0}{1+{e}^{-0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a897637f-a103-5c3f-81b6-65711f8a97e5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a897637f-a103-5c3f-81b6-65711f8a97e5" :answer-field/id #uuid "a897637f-a103-5c3f-81b6-65711f8a97e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f869162a-a3a8-5474-8b17-6aeb207f63c0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d226f22a-73aa-5bd5-8ffb-659b107ef567" "answer-6098c79c-346b-5248-8398-6ba51720d41a" "answer-f869162a-a3a8-5474-8b17-6aeb207f63c0" "answer-4238841a-e6fd-5b61-9bb7-9b81cecfd441" "answer-58c5d980-f308-55bb-b6dc-33f198a88f15"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d226f22a-73aa-5bd5-8ffb-659b107ef567" :answer/id #uuid "d226f22a-73aa-5bd5-8ffb-659b107ef567" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6098c79c-346b-5248-8398-6ba51720d41a" :answer/id #uuid "6098c79c-346b-5248-8398-6ba51720d41a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f869162a-a3a8-5474-8b17-6aeb207f63c0" :answer/id #uuid "f869162a-a3a8-5474-8b17-6aeb207f63c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4238841a-e6fd-5b61-9bb7-9b81cecfd441" :answer/id #uuid "4238841a-e6fd-5b61-9bb7-9b81cecfd441" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58c5d980-f308-55bb-b6dc-33f198a88f15" :answer/id #uuid "58c5d980-f308-55bb-b6dc-33f198a88f15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-df476431-ab3a-5147-98f8-ef5f1e16d04c" :question/id #uuid "df476431-ab3a-5147-98f8-ef5f1e16d04c" :question/math-academy-id "q-353353" :question/problem "![](images/85/853358cc3207d3f2738ecc3bd2ee6391d62b1a51735c43e16f37a2b83414800e.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t+1),\\,y=t{e}^{t},\\,-\\frac{1}{3}<t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\nshown above, calculate the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=0.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$m=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{3}{3t+1},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=(t+1){e}^{t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{(t+1){e}^{t}}{(\\frac{3}{3t+1})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(t+1)(3t+1){e}^{t}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=0,$ the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{dy}{dx}\\,{|}_{t\\,=\\,0} & =\\frac{(0+1)(0+1){e}^{0}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8b9a1810-6a6d-5eb5-883e-8d03107298a3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8b9a1810-6a6d-5eb5-883e-8d03107298a3" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b9a1810-6a6d-5eb5-883e-8d03107298a3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e9f8b02c-3c71-509f-93de-e4a3c2bb07cb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e9f8b02c-3c71-509f-93de-e4a3c2bb07cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9f8b02c-3c71-509f-93de-e4a3c2bb07cb" :answer/id #uuid "e9f8b02c-3c71-509f-93de-e4a3c2bb07cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-21abfc2b-1c65-57da-8fcf-53cc0cb791f0" :question/id #uuid "21abfc2b-1c65-57da-8fcf-53cc0cb791f0"] ["question-21abfc2b-1c65-57da-8fcf-53cc0cb791f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-6840"] ["question-21abfc2b-1c65-57da-8fcf-53cc0cb791f0" :question/problem "For the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$"] ["question-21abfc2b-1c65-57da-8fcf-53cc0cb791f0" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}=-\\frac{3}{t\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+1}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =-\\,\\frac{3}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}+1} \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{3}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\cdot 0+1} \\\\  & =-\\,3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-21abfc2b-1c65-57da-8fcf-53cc0cb791f0" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-3bfbeb97-b5a7-5edb-811c-c6fd832edf47" :answer-field/id #uuid "3bfbeb97-b5a7-5edb-811c-c6fd832edf47"] ["answer-16e9c511-8886-5f56-8ee7-6556baca60f7" :answer/id #uuid "16e9c511-8886-5f56-8ee7-6556baca60f7"] ["answer-16e9c511-8886-5f56-8ee7-6556baca60f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-16e9c511-8886-5f56-8ee7-6556baca60f7" :answer/value "-1"] ["answer-e0c0fa7e-1c3b-5c73-8f6c-dd538719b8ec" :answer/id #uuid "e0c0fa7e-1c3b-5c73-8f6c-dd538719b8ec"] ["answer-e0c0fa7e-1c3b-5c73-8f6c-dd538719b8ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e0c0fa7e-1c3b-5c73-8f6c-dd538719b8ec" :answer/value "-3"] ["answer-9f3946a4-4840-5c17-bc49-b6cd5ef2faaf" :answer/id #uuid "9f3946a4-4840-5c17-bc49-b6cd5ef2faaf"] ["answer-9f3946a4-4840-5c17-bc49-b6cd5ef2faaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9f3946a4-4840-5c17-bc49-b6cd5ef2faaf" :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{1}{3\\pi +1}"] ["answer-2ef85eba-7368-57c1-8685-8d542b3d4d4c" :answer/id #uuid "2ef85eba-7368-57c1-8685-8d542b3d4d4c"] ["answer-2ef85eba-7368-57c1-8685-8d542b3d4d4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2ef85eba-7368-57c1-8685-8d542b3d4d4c" :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{1}{\\pi +1}"] ["answer-f30dcc98-6482-51c6-8828-44cf84a10887" :answer/id #uuid "f30dcc98-6482-51c6-8828-44cf84a10887"] ["answer-f30dcc98-6482-51c6-8828-44cf84a10887" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f30dcc98-6482-51c6-8828-44cf84a10887" :answer/value "-\\,\\frac{3}{\\pi }"] ["answer-field-3bfbeb97-b5a7-5edb-811c-c6fd832edf47" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-3bfbeb97-b5a7-5edb-811c-c6fd832edf47" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-3bfbeb97-b5a7-5edb-811c-c6fd832edf47" :answer-field/correct "answer-e0c0fa7e-1c3b-5c73-8f6c-dd538719b8ec"] ["answer-field-3bfbeb97-b5a7-5edb-811c-c6fd832edf47" :answer-field/choices "answer-16e9c511-8886-5f56-8ee7-6556baca60f7"] ["answer-field-3bfbeb97-b5a7-5edb-811c-c6fd832edf47" :answer-field/choices "answer-e0c0fa7e-1c3b-5c73-8f6c-dd538719b8ec"] ["answer-field-3bfbeb97-b5a7-5edb-811c-c6fd832edf47" :answer-field/choices "answer-9f3946a4-4840-5c17-bc49-b6cd5ef2faaf"] ["answer-field-3bfbeb97-b5a7-5edb-811c-c6fd832edf47" :answer-field/choices "answer-2ef85eba-7368-57c1-8685-8d542b3d4d4c"] ["answer-field-3bfbeb97-b5a7-5edb-811c-c6fd832edf47" :answer-field/choices "answer-f30dcc98-6482-51c6-8828-44cf84a10887"] ["question-21abfc2b-1c65-57da-8fcf-53cc0cb791f0" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-3bfbeb97-b5a7-5edb-811c-c6fd832edf47"] [17592186083240 :knowledge-point/questions "question-21abfc2b-1c65-57da-8fcf-53cc0cb791f0"] ["question-7c906060-00dc-59ed-b471-aa166bd736b1" :question/id #uuid "7c906060-00dc-59ed-b471-aa166bd736b1"] ["question-7c906060-00dc-59ed-b471-aa166bd736b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-20987"] ["question-7c906060-00dc-59ed-b471-aa166bd736b1" :question/problem "![](images/b1/b165889c6169a417f4d56f544aec8a049685693ff2b01ea13d51a9f4d841be4c.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx={t}^{3}-t,\\,y={t}^{2}-4,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\n find the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=3.$"] ["question-7c906060-00dc-59ed-b471-aa166bd736b1" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{t}^{2}-1,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2t}{3{t}^{2}-1}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=3$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{2\\cdot 3}{3({3}^{2})-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{27-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-7c906060-00dc-59ed-b471-aa166bd736b1" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-4988bf56-303b-59a6-9f79-eb24f4974217" :answer-field/id #uuid "4988bf56-303b-59a6-9f79-eb24f4974217"] ["answer-5f5471cf-39c9-57da-8b25-92ea610ee7b8" :answer/id #uuid "5f5471cf-39c9-57da-8b25-92ea610ee7b8"] ["answer-5f5471cf-39c9-57da-8b25-92ea610ee7b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5f5471cf-39c9-57da-8b25-92ea610ee7b8" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}"] ["answer-1b2ee053-4ac9-5907-8967-107610ee1cf5" :answer/id #uuid "1b2ee053-4ac9-5907-8967-107610ee1cf5"] ["answer-1b2ee053-4ac9-5907-8967-107610ee1cf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1b2ee053-4ac9-5907-8967-107610e